(2289864, 312856, 24212, '<td valign="top">I noticed this last night, but was too late to vote/comment. This one stood out from all the thumbnails, so I had a quick look. At first, I thought that the blurring had been done in PS, but I can see some dust spots in the shot (presumably from stopping down to get a longer shutter speed) that are not blurred.<br/> <br/>Fantastic panning and a great sense of fun conveyed. Love the colours.</td>', 'I noticed this last night, but was too late to vote/comment. This one stood out from all the thumbnails, so I had a quick look. At first, I thought that the blurring had been done in PS, but I can see some dust spots in the shot (presumably from stopping down to get a longer shutter speed) that are not blurred. Fantastic panning and a great sense of fun conveyed. Love the colours.', '2006-04-05 15:29:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2289984, 312827, 55025, '<td valign="top">Nice photo.</td>', 'Nice photo.', '2006-04-05 16:18:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2290009, 313214, 5112, '<td valign="top">Thank you!<br/> <br/>@Steve - clarify under contrast (I think) in PaintShop Pro, it increases contrast.  It has 5 settings, and you can use it on an image more than once.  It''s the lazy way to increase contrast.  2 is the default setting.  I am very lazy when it comes to editing.</td>', 'Thank you! @Steve - clarify under contrast (I think) in PaintShop Pro, it increases contrast.  It has 5 settings, and you can use it on an image more than once.  It''s the lazy way to increase contrast.  2 is the default setting.  I am very lazy when it comes to editing.', '2006-04-05 16:28:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2290296, 310755, 11895, '<td valign="top">This shot has a very real feeling to it, natural light and not a set-up.  I love it, and am glad that it ribboned.</td>', 'This shot has a very real feeling to it, natural light and not a set-up.  I love it, and am glad that it ribboned.', '2006-04-05 19:24:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2290320, 312507, 53887, '<td valign="top">Its a good idea but i think its time for a new camera. Your cell phone just didn''t cut it for this shit. I also think that it would have done better if the legs were a little darker as in the other copy of this pictue. It didn''t show as much of the distracting noise. But the idea was good. keep up the good work.</td>', 'Its a good idea but i think its time for a new camera. Your cell phone just didn''t cut it for this shit. I also think that it would have done better if the legs were a little darker as in the other copy of this pictue. It didn''t show as much of the distracting noise. But the idea was good. keep up the good work.', '2006-04-05 19:36:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2290457, 312868, 3306, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on yet another ribbon. You have a talent for capturing the joys of childhood in a very unique and captivating manner.</td>', 'Congratulations on yet another ribbon. You have a talent for capturing the joys of childhood in a very unique and captivating manner.', '2006-04-05 20:35:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2290463, 312827, 3306, '<td valign="top">Wow, a blue ribbon on your first submission. Congratulations. You make it look easy.</td>', 'Wow, a blue ribbon on your first submission. Congratulations. You make it look easy.', '2006-04-05 20:38:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2290489, 313015, 54811, '<td valign="top">Just a follow up on how I took this shot.  Nothing special really.  No flash involved.  Just put camera on a tripod focused at the balls using a 1 second exposure, the lighting is coming from an overhead can light in the ceiling.  Just set the camera timer, and went to the other end of the table and hit the cue ball really slowly once the timer went off.<br/> <br/>I probably should have done some work in photoshop on the picture, but all I did was  resize to 640 wide and submit it.</td>', 'Just a follow up on how I took this shot.  Nothing special really.  No flash involved.  Just put camera on a tripod focused at the balls using a 1 second exposure, the lighting is coming from an overhead can light in the ceiling.  Just set the camera timer, and went to the other end of the table and hit the cue ball really slowly once the timer went off. I probably should have done some work in photoshop on the picture, but all I did was  resize to 640 wide and submit it.', '2006-04-05 20:50:59.000000', NULL, 0),
