(2295996, 312853, 47117, '<td valign="top">Shutterpug, the man on the left IS the same man. This was a long exposure, and I wanted him to be more out of focus on the left because "that" was the "subconcious" part of him.  <br/> <br/>You REALLY need to stop following my photos around and giving bad commentary on them.  You are developing quite a pattern for yourself which I find embarrassing for you.</td>', 'Shutterpug, the man on the left IS the same man. This was a long exposure, and I wanted him to be more out of focus on the left because "that" was the "subconcious" part of him.   You REALLY need to stop following my photos around and giving bad commentary on them.  You are developing quite a pattern for yourself which I find embarrassing for you.', '2006-04-07 19:29:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2296026, 312853, 47117, '<td valign="top">How this was done:<br/> <br/>30 second exposure set with timer.<br/> <br/>Lights on, shutter clicks.  10 seconds in, shut off light, subject moves to other side of table. Last 10 seconds, light is flicked back on.<br/> <br/>During the last 10 seconds, I had the subject move slightly to cause the blur, giving the illusion of the subconcious over the more sharp first shot, the concious, hence the title.<br/> <br/>To those that wondered how it was done, thank you for the compliments. I hope you can try different ideas as well using long exposures. It is really a lot of fun, and there are many such shots on the site that have long exposures using the same person in them.  They are cool to look at as well.<br/> <br/>Only three shots were taken for this entry, and out of that three only the one I could actually use.  I had other ideas, but didn''t have the time to produce them that evening.  <br/> <br/>Thanks for the compliments!<br/> <br/>Rose  <br/> <br/></td>', 'How this was done: 30 second exposure set with timer. Lights on, shutter clicks.  10 seconds in, shut off light, subject moves to other side of table. Last 10 seconds, light is flicked back on. During the last 10 seconds, I had the subject move slightly to cause the blur, giving the illusion of the subconcious over the more sharp first shot, the concious, hence the title. To those that wondered how it was done, thank you for the compliments. I hope you can try different ideas as well using long exposures. It is really a lot of fun, and there are many such shots on the site that have long exposures using the same person in them.  They are cool to look at as well. Only three shots were taken for this entry, and out of that three only the one I could actually use.  I had other ideas, but didn''t have the time to produce them that evening.   Thanks for the compliments! Rose   ', '2006-04-07 19:45:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2296074, 313242, 2158, '<td valign="top">I really expected this to do better.</td>', 'I really expected this to do better.', '2006-04-07 20:14:02.000000', NULL, 0),
